1. SQL
------
SQL (Structured Query Language) is a standard language used to create, manage, manipulate, and retrieve data from relational databases.

-----------------------------------------

2. Database
-----------
A database is an organized collection of related data that can be easily accessed, managed, and updated.

-----------------------------------------

3. Table
--------
A table stores data in rows and columns.

-----------------------------------------

4. Row (Record)
---------------
A row represents a single record in a table.

-----------------------------------------

5. Column (Field)
-----------------
A column represents a specific attribute or property of the data.

-----------------------------------------

6. Primary Key
--------------
A Primary Key uniquely identifies each record in a table. It cannot contain NULL or duplicate values.

-----------------------------------------

7. Foreign Key
--------------
A Foreign Key creates a relationship between two tables by referring to the Primary Key of another table.

-----------------------------------------

8. Candidate Key
----------------
A Candidate Key is a column (or set of columns) that can uniquely identify a record. One candidate key is chosen as the Primary Key.

-----------------------------------------

9. Composite Key
----------------
A Composite Key consists of two or more columns that together uniquely identify a record.

-----------------------------------------

10. Super Key
-------------
A Super Key is one or more columns that uniquely identify a row in a table.

-----------------------------------------

11. Alternate Key
-----------------
Candidate keys that are not selected as the Primary Key are called Alternate Keys.

-----------------------------------------

12. Constraint
--------------
Constraints are rules applied to columns to ensure data accuracy and integrity.

Types:
• PRIMARY KEY
• FOREIGN KEY
• UNIQUE
• NOT NULL
• CHECK
• DEFAULT

-----------------------------------------

13. DDL (Data Definition Language)
----------------------------------
Used to define and modify database structures.

Commands:
CREATE
ALTER
DROP
TRUNCATE
RENAME

-----------------------------------------

14. DML (Data Manipulation Language)
------------------------------------
Used to manipulate data inside tables.

Commands:
INSERT
UPDATE
DELETE

-----------------------------------------

15. DQL (Data Query Language)
-----------------------------
Used to retrieve data from the database.

Command:
SELECT

-----------------------------------------

16. TCL (Transaction Control Language)
----------------------------------------
Used to manage transactions.

Commands:
COMMIT
ROLLBACK
SAVEPOINT

-----------------------------------------

17. DCL (Data Control Language)
-------------------------------
Used to control user permissions.

Commands:
GRANT
REVOKE

-----------------------------------------

