-----------------------------------------

23. ORDER BY
------------
Sorts the result in ascending (ASC) or descending (DESC) order.

-----------------------------------------

24. GROUP BY
------------
Groups rows that have the same values in specified columns.

-----------------------------------------

25. HAVING
----------
Filters grouped data after GROUP BY.

-----------------------------------------

26. WHERE
----------
Filters rows before grouping.

-----------------------------------------

27. JOIN
--------
A JOIN combines rows from two or more tables.

Types:
• INNER JOIN
• LEFT JOIN
• RIGHT JOIN
• CROSS JOIN
• SELF JOIN

-----------------------------------------

28. Subquery
------------
A query written inside another SQL query.

-----------------------------------------

29. View
--------
A View is a virtual table created using a SELECT statement.

-----------------------------------------

30. Index
---------
An Index improves the speed of data retrieval.

-----------------------------------------

31. Stored Procedure
--------------------
A Stored Procedure is a saved SQL program that performs a specific task.

-----------------------------------------

32. Function
------------
A Function accepts input, performs a calculation, and returns a single value.

-----------------------------------------

33. Trigger
-----------
A Trigger automatically executes when INSERT, UPDATE, or DELETE operations occur.

-----------------------------------------

34. Transaction
---------------
A Transaction is a sequence of SQL statements executed as a single unit of work.

-----------------------------------------

35. ACID Properties
-------------------
Atomicity
Consistency
Isolation
Durability

-----------------------------------------

36. CTE (Common Table Expression)
---------------------------------
A temporary result set that can be referenced within a SQL statement using the WITH clause.

-----------------------------------------

37. Window Function
-------------------
Performs calculations across a set of rows without grouping them.

Examples:
ROW_NUMBER()
RANK()
DENSE_RANK()
LAG()
LEAD()

-----------------------------------------

38. Normalization
-----------------
The process of organizing data to reduce redundancy and improve data integrity.

-----------------------------------------

39. Denormalization
-------------------
Combining tables or adding redundant data to improve query performance.

-----------------------------------------

40. Schema
----------
A Schema is the logical structure of a database containing tables, views, procedures, functions, and other objects.

